      porQueImporta: 'A refinery shutdown is not a scandal: it is necessary maintenance, and deferring it costs more. But for months the country bought abroad the fuel it makes, with a cost for the halted production estimated in the hundreds of millions of dollars. That cost ends up reflected in the price of petrol and diesel.',
